Here is the commit message:
SOLR-5231: Fixed a bug with the behavior of BoolField that
 caused documents w/o a value for the field to act as if the value were true
 in functions if no other documents in the same index segment had a value of
 true.

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1521948 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the default handling of Boolean field values in documents that do not explicitly have a value set. Specifically, when no documents in the same index segment had a value of true, documents without a value were incorrectly treated as if they had a true value. This led to unexpected behavior in functions that operated on these fields.

