int tord = -2;
...
return sindex.getOrd(doc) == trueOrd;
```
Reason:
The variable `tord` is now initialized to `-2`, which denotes a missing value explicitly. This change ensures that documents without a value will not be treated as having a true value, as they will not match the new `trueOrd`, thus correcting the erroneous behavior in functions that operate on these fields.


